    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense hinges on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** today, who remains our clear anchor with a 78.53 efficiency score. Despite facing a lefty in Rod\u00f3n, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.33 xERA matchup and an elite xwOBA profile, making him a must-start despite the handedness disadvantage. Following him, **Josh Lowe** stands out as the most intriguing value at a 64.48 score; while he is currently projected in the #9 hole\u2014which drags his floor\u2014his dynamic platoon advantage against Severino provides enough upside to justify a strong start, assuming the lineup projection holds.\n\nThe benching decision for the day was relatively straightforward given the team's health landscape, though **Dominic Smith** barely secured his spot over prospective fringe depth. With **Luis Robert Jr.** officially sidelined on the IL and superstars like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill** caught in an off-day cycle, the roster is currently thinned out. **Nasim Nunez** (49.48) sits firmly in \"marginal\" territory; while his elite sprint speed is a constant target for our SB-focused build, the combination of a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a tough matchup against Peterson\u2019s L/L profile caps his ceiling. \n\nManagement must remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Lowe**. While both are projected to start, any downward shift in their respective batting orders would immediately compress their scores. **Liam Hicks** (52.47) and **Dominic Smith** (53.85) provide stability, but they are playing against high-leverage arms like Strider and Alcantara, necessitating a close watch on late-breaking weather reports or defensive substitution risks that could shorten their plate appearances.",
